# PHP extraction and strangler patches

## Smallest possible facade patch

When patching a facade (e.g. `include/class.sla.php`):

- Preserve the existing entry-point **method signature** exactly.
- Preserve existing **side effects** and facade-level orchestration (globals, schedule resolution, caching, caller-visible contracts).
- Move only the core logic delegation into the extracted service.

## Anti-recursion

The extracted service must **never** call back into the facade entry point it replaces. That causes infinite recursion after the strangler patch.

Choose one pattern:

- **Lifted logic** — hold the exact inline expression/operators from the original method body.
- **Forward delegation** — call deeper, unrelated methods/classes only (never the facade entry point).

## Touch only manifest-named files

Only modify files named in the current seam manifest:

- `extractionTarget` — new or updated service under `include/Services/`
- `facadeFile` — facade to patch

Do not refactor unrelated PHP in the same change.
